## ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## Notch — .gitignore
## Based on github/gitignore Swift.gitignore + Xcode additions.
## Xcode generates a lot of noise; this keeps the history readable.
## ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon
._*
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.fseventsd
.Spotlight-V100
.TemporaryItems
.Trashes
.VolumeIcon.icns

## Xcode — user-specific state
## xcuserdata holds breakpoints, window layout, and scheme selection.
## Never commit it: it churns on every build and conflicts constantly.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout
*.moved-aside
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

## Xcode — build products
build/
DerivedData/
*.o
*.LinkFileList
*.swiftmodule

## Xcode — Playgrounds
timeline.xctimeline
playground.xcworkspace

## Swift Package Manager
## Package.resolved IS committed for apps (it pins exact dependency versions
## so CI and your machine build the same thing). It is NOT committed for
## libraries. Notch is an app, so it stays tracked — hence no ignore line.
.build/
.swiftpm/
Packages/
*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/

## CocoaPods / Carthage — not used, but ignore in case a dependency drags one in
Pods/
Carthage/Build/

## Fastlane — not used yet, likely in Phase 3 for TestFlight uploads
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
fastlane/test_output

## ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## Secrets — see docs/security/secrets.md
## Nothing in this section should ever reach a commit. The rules here are
## belt-and-braces: the real control is that API keys live only in Supabase
## Edge Function environment variables, never in the app bundle or the repo.
## ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
Secrets.swift
Secrets.xcconfig
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
supabase/.env
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/

## ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## Spikes — throwaway code, but their *outputs* are the deliverable
## ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## Python (vision accuracy harness)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

## Your own meal photos are personal data — never push them.
## The ground-truth CSV and the generated report ARE committed:
## the measured baseline is a Phase 0 exit criterion.
spikes/vision-accuracy/photos/*
!spikes/vision-accuracy/photos/.gitkeep
spikes/vision-accuracy/.cache/
spikes/vision-accuracy/runs/*
!spikes/vision-accuracy/runs/.gitkeep

## Your own HealthKit exports are personal data
spikes/healthkit/exports/

## Regenerable spike fixtures (python3 make_fixtures.py) — not worth versioning
spikes/vision-accuracy/fixtures/
